#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100647 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "a0f21b4c-0f5c-5567-aaec-9da481d2e7ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-547" :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100648 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "0c84fc6d-422e-5729-94d2-a12cda71f78d" :question/math-academy-id "e-548" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100649 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "244bb10c-4c6f-5be0-bd9a-72b4defee245" :question/math-academy-id "e-549" :question/problem "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100650 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "a1572338-79f7-5da7-b9f6-552dcb7984a6" :question/math-academy-id "e-550" :question/problem "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c6edbe-0d21-5292-af54-3aee476000ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} {:answer/id #uuid "93a81b6f-340c-5a38-93ca-46a5ff16f29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342311} {:answer/id #uuid "2383bcff-b9da-593f-88c2-e89a2f61299a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342312} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca59082-0a28-52be-80e6-2e8a54550b5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342313} {:answer/id #uuid "8a29d6a2-873c-5695-b181-655cccae2a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c6edbe-0d21-5292-af54-3aee476000ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342310} :answer-field/id #uuid "40a81efe-bb81-5712-8a60-556d0e16bd14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ba1202f-23bb-59b7-8a58-51ad745d9aba" :question/math-academy-id "q-15225" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/6c70d5f15424c4d7d67a3998a785a214e46e8dfa47b83839fd99a574b2f756cf.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[-1,6]$, is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(4,0)$ with radius $1.$ Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5].$" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-0}\\cdot (3+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{\\pi }{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a9cb877-f670-5acc-be10-454cec272525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099212} {:answer/id #uuid "e8090f80-705e-5379-9f3d-5e9d20ce0098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099213} {:answer/id #uuid "fc399a7d-96fe-5e54-9af7-f48f16fa8fe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099214} {:answer/id #uuid "65106760-2d63-5dd2-a3d5-5e0e8d3d1de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099215} {:answer/id #uuid "781b84f8-7658-5344-b5c8-a8ee9e808812" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8090f80-705e-5379-9f3d-5e9d20ce0098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099213} :answer-field/id #uuid "64ca97ca-0196-5ed0-8abe-82f6d68edd1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099211}] :question/id #uuid "28111792-cb9a-53d6-8e29-9d2f2d29b33c" :question/math-academy-id "q-2491" :question/problem "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x) = 3x^{2}$ on the interval $[- 2, 2]$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "672e9ba0-e2be-5a8f-a78a-6bb819f35c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291195} {:answer/id #uuid "f49fc375-5782-572e-8f2c-7a9cf21ca337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291196} {:answer/id #uuid "9695b549-f9eb-58e7-b607-8000ed32121d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291197} {:answer/id #uuid "b99675fb-9a01-5b54-8ba3-4589872f6cd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291198} {:answer/id #uuid "6871dfb7-e709-540e-bc17-835ef63ad935" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9695b549-f9eb-58e7-b607-8000ed32121d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291197} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ae9fb8-6a3d-58fa-892f-b68188b64c4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41a9e5db-75da-5502-afac-88828e98449b" :question/math-academy-id "q-30776" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $g(x)=2{x}^{3}-x-1$ on the interval $[-2,0].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{0-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(2{x}^{3}-x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x)|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}-0)-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{2}-(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(8-2+2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-8) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53eb00fe-4f55-552c-8c93-84099ec474f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53eb00fe-4f55-552c-8c93-84099ec474f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291205} :answer-field/id #uuid "60610310-2ac4-5ae9-a341-f1deb1d8f329" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e56f391c-b858-5626-9202-9c04093762c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-316307" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/64682c2166e3f9fd2366f925330d04f95b54f370fd3d887d1d8aef8885ac35ec.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-8,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $20$, $80$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-20+80-10=50.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-8)}\\cdot (50) \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c039ea78-e776-5206-8e89-f17e9e3aa758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291229} {:answer/id #uuid "9debab67-805d-5409-b59d-638c831040c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9debab67-805d-5409-b59d-638c831040c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291230} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b1da21-91a7-5b46-85c0-256a1c75b6d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bfc3ffe0-eb79-55a0-9876-0723bc5ad393" :question/math-academy-id "q-344596" :question/problem "The **exact** value of $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-8x-10$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12$ is\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(6{x}^{2}-8x-10)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(2{c}^{3}-4{c}^{2}-10c)-0] \\\\ -12 & =2{c}^{2}-4c-10 \\\\ 0 & =2{c}^{2}-4c+2 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-2c+1 \\\\ 0 & =(c-1)^{2} \\\\ c & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27b54b43-3c84-5656-be36-ea9c956fb491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27b54b43-3c84-5656-be36-ea9c956fb491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291240} :answer-field/id #uuid "43776673-5b88-5afd-9826-30b5c8f2c3f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "752704cb-a8ad-55ac-ac26-51b58834ab35" :question/math-academy-id "q-344648" :question/problem "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)={cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ on the interval $[0,\\pi ].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this integral using a substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{-1}{u}^{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{{u}^{7}}{7})|}_{1}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }[(-1)^{7}-{1}^{7}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6441432-c33b-55f9-8ad3-ece97b055c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6441432-c33b-55f9-8ad3-ece97b055c92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342321} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cdfcd64-e975-5f9a-a87e-656249c63b24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f43cc69-bbf5-5e06-8e03-26d2b66ad73a" :question/math-academy-id "q-344702" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062030/assets/8ddd8493662174e0ddaf9bdd63b0ec382f6bb25c9079f1a339b71400b8cf3860.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-6,6],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $15$, $60$ and $9,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-6,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-15+60-9=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-(-6)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
